\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Disjunctive graph of a job shop with two jobs. Solid arrows are the precedences within the jobs ($a_1 \to a_2 \to a_3$ and $b_1 \to b_2$). The dashed and dotted double arrows link the pairs of activities that share a machine: $a_1$ and $b_2$ on $M_1$, $a_2$ and $b_1$ on $M_2$; $a_3$ is alone on $M_3$ and needs no disjunctive arc. Choosing an orientation for each pair produces a schedule.}}{12}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
